{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry things are slow today. I checked your computer and it has plenty of free disk space, so that isn't the cause. To narrow it down, could you tell me: (1) Are you in the office today or working from home on VPN? (2) Is it only the shared drives that are slow, or are websites and Teams slow too? (3) Is it one particular shared folder, and are coworkers nearby seeing the same slowness? While you check, these often help: if you're on Wi-Fi, move closer to the access point or plug in a network cable. Pause any big uploads or downloads, like OneDrive sync or cloud backups. If you're on VPN, disconnect it and connect again. Shared drives are slower over VPN by design, so large files open faster from OneDrive or SharePoint. If you haven't fully restarted your computer in a few days, do a full restart. Let me know how it goes and what you find.",
  "internal_note": "KB-015 quick checks. User: James O'Connor (id 8), Operations, Warehouse Supervisor, active account, no lockouts. Device BL-DT-0108 (desktop): 78% disk free, no warnings, but it shows OFFLINE with last check-in 2026-10-09 12:53 UTC. That may just mean it's switched off, or he may be working on another machine. Sign-ins: usually alternates between corporate network (m365 from 203.0.113.10) and home VPN (residential 198.51.100.28). All normal: Chicago only, Duo MFA, within usual hours. Nothing suggests a compromise. Waiting on the user to tell us: office or VPN, only shares or everything slow, which share, and whether others are affected. Escalate to Tier 2 per KB-015 if the whole office is slow or one share is slow for everyone. If only this device is slow after the fixes and a restart, follow KB-019.",
